   "answer": "No plasmid lowered the growth rate of this host. Every 95% confidence interval of the relative rate holds 1, and every p value is 0.2432 or higher. I removed the unsupported \"10% to 25%\" range from my earlier text. I also corrected how I described the blocks.\n\n**What I did**\n1. I fitted a logistic curve to each of the 70 wells with growthcurver 4.6.1 (step: fit_growth_curves). The time unit is hours and t_trim is 0, so all readings were used.\n2. The background correction was \"min\". I set no blank wells.\n3. I excluded 14 wells: W10 to W18 (block 2) and W80 to W84 (block 12). You gave the exclusion list but no reasons. Blocks 2 and 12 are gone completely, host wells included.\n4. I divided the r of each plasmid well by the r of the Host well in the same block (step: compare_growth). Host is the reference.\n5. One replicate is one well. The n for each plasmid is 5 wells, one in each of 5 different blocks. Plasmids P1 to P8 sit in blocks 1, 3, 7, 8 and 9. Plasmids P9, P10, P11 and P14 sit in blocks 4, 5, 6, 10 and 11. Host has n = 10, one well in each of those 10 blocks. I do not know if the blocks come from independent cultures.\n\nThe plot shows each curve reaching a plateau and the fit following the readings. No well had a growthcurver note. Some wells have a small shoulder or overshoot near OD 0.4 to 0.5, for example W68 and W77. These wells fit less well.\n\n**Results**\n- Mean r of the Host wells is 0.3805 per h (n 10).\n- Fitted r ranged from 0.2881 to 0.4794 per h across wells. The median doubling time was 1.828 h.\n- I did not request the lag time, so I did not run it.\n\nThe table shows the relative r for each plasmid (mean, 95% confidence interval) and the p value of the two-sided one-sample t test against 1. Each plasmid has n = 5.\n\n| Plasmid | Relative r | 95% CI | p |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | 1.005 | 0.9079 to 1.103 | 0.8872 |\n| P2 | 1.028 | 0.9192 to 1.136 | 0.5171 |\n| P3 | 1.033 | 0.9183 to 1.148 | 0.4697 |\n| P4 | 0.9657 | 0.7957 to 1.136 | 0.6052 |\n| P5 | 1.072 | 0.9254 to 1.22 | 0.2432 |\n| P6 | 1.008 | 0.8973 to 1.119 | 0.8458 |\n| P7 | 0.9612 | 0.8129 to 1.109 | 0.5077 |\n| P8 | 0.9754 | 0.8915 to 1.059 | 0.4626 |\n| P9 | 1.043 | 0.8602 to 1.225 | 0.5522 |\n| P10 | 0.9902 | 0.8293 to 1.151 | 0.8734 |\n| P11 | 0.9466 | 0.7424 to 1.151 | 0.5076 |\n| P14 | 1.082 | 0.8864 to 1.278 | 0.3090 |\n\nThe mean of the 12 plasmid means is 1.009 (step: calculate).\n\n**What I infer**\n- The point estimates of P4, P7, P8 and P11 are below 1, from 0.9466 to 0.9754. The intervals are wide and hold 1. This is not evidence of a lower rate.\n- The intervals for some plasmids are wide. For P11 the interval is 0.7424 to 1.151. With n = 5 the data cannot exclude a rate change inside such an interval, in either direction.\n- The mean of the plasmid means is close to 1. The plasmids as a group do not change the host growth rate in this experiment.\n- I ran 12 tests and did not correct for multiple tests. A correction would only make the result less significant.\n\n**What is uncertain**\n- The wells in each block can be technical replicates of one culture. If so, the n of 5 does not show biological variation.\n- The \"min\" background correction shifts each well by its own minimum. The file already starts at 0. I do not know if the harness chose \"min\" or if you did.\n- Blocks 2 and 12 are excluded, so each plasmid rests on 5 blocks.\n\n**What waits for the scientist**\n- The reason for the excluded wells, so I can record it.\n- Whether the blocks are independent cultures.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Background correction: min · Medium-only wells for the blank: none · Last time point of the fit: 0 · Unit of the time column: h · Wells that you exclude: W10, W11, W12, W13, W14, W15, W16, W17, W18, W80, W81, W82, W83, W84 · Points in each window of the lag time method: 5 · Reference strain or condition: Host · Divide by the reference mean or by the reference well of the same block: same block.",
